<title>USA: San Fran zoo pledges discounts if bond passes.</title>
<headline>San Fran zoo pledges discounts if bond passes.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zoo officials have pledged to give San Francisco residents a 25 percent discount on admissions if a $48 million bond issue passes June 3, according to a published report Wednesday.</p>
<p>The discount was announced at a hearing called by Supervisor Tom Ammiano to ask San Francisco zoo what benefits it would provide city residents who are being asked to support the bonds, San Francisco Chronicle reported.</p>
<p>The discount would take effect about 18 months after the June election, when the first new major animal exhibit opens.</p>
<p>The bond proceeds would fund several zoo projects.</p>
</text>
